Naxsi is a web application firewall for nginx.  Instead of a signature
list it works the other way round: requests are scored against a small
set of rules that describe suspicious characters and patterns, and a
request is refused once its score passes the configured limit.

Whitelists cover the places where an application legitimately uses such
characters, and a learning mode collects the candidates for them from
real traffic.

This port only installs the module sources and the upstream rule sets.
The module itself is built by the nginx ports when their NAXSI option
is enabled.
